# R-60.1: files hashed on their BYTES are stored byte-for-byte (no end-of-line conversion),
# so a checkout on any platform reproduces the hash.  Canonical-serialisation digests
# (config_dict sha256) are EOL-invariant and need nothing.
*.json      -text
*.sha256    -text
*FROZEN*.md -text
# byte-hashed by REGISTRATION_SHA256 (campaign_config_v5.py:978, v6.py:1521: preregistration_v5_DRAFT.md)
preregistration_*.md -text
*.parquet   binary
*.npz       binary
# byte-hashed by ball_socket/memory_sign.assert_src_identity against Paper 2's copy
src/rheology.py -text